# staticrypt scratch dir. share_publish.py used to encrypt inside the working
# tree of this PUBLIC repo, so every page was committed twice — once published
# at the root, once under .staging/out/ — and each page passed through here as
# plaintext for the moment staticrypt took to read it. The job now works in
# ~/.config/being/share-staging, outside the repo. This entry stays as
# belt-and-braces: `git add -A` must never pick that directory up again.
.staging/
